dough that is stuffed and baked over a wood fire, soft inside and crispy outside. Unlike pizza, Medfouna consists of two layers of dough: one at the bottom and one on top that covers the filling. It is typically served along with a glass of Moroccan mint tea."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-medfouna"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medfouna"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Moroccan cuisine","cuisine/moroccan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"My Moroccan Food","ref":"site/mymoroccanfood-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"mymoroccanfood.com","note":"Moroccan recipe blog linked to cookbook author Nargisse Benkabbou, covering breads, soups and tagines.","url":"https://www.mymoroccanfood.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Taste of Maroc","ref":"site/tasteofmaroc-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"tasteofmaroc.com","note":"Moroccan recipes and tutorials from Christine Benlafquih, formerly the Moroccan food writer at The Spruce Eats.","url":"https://tasteofmaroc.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"},{"name":"Salima's Kitchen","ref":"site/salimaskitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"salimaskitchen.com","note":"Moroccan section of Salima Benkhalti's blog, drawing on her family cooking.","url":"https://salimaskitchen.com/category/moroccan/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Moroccan cuisine","links":[["Babbouche","dish/babbouche"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Couscous","dish/couscous"],["Harira","dish/harira"],["Kourdass","dish/kourdass"],["Mhancha","dish/mhancha"],["Pastilla","dish/pastilla"],["Sellou","dish/sellou"],["Tajine lham-lahlou","dish/tajine-lham-lahlou"],["Taktouka","dish/taktouka"],["Tehane","dish/tehane"],["Zaazaa","dish/zaazaa"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/ef/Medfouna_or_Berber_Pizza_at_a_local_restaurant_near_Merzouga%2C_Errachidia%2C_Morocco.jpg/500px-Medfouna_or_Berber_Pizza_at_a_local_rest